 A full Android/NDK Gradle build was attempted, but this working environment does not contain the
 Gradle 8.10.2 distribution and cannot download it. The current build-validation gap is therefore
 an environment limitation, not a reported compiler result.
+
+## Stage 2 — guest GPU ABI split (implemented)
+
+Stage 2 stops treating every Mali device as if the same Linux Vulkan driver could drive it.
+
+### Runtime backend selection
+
+`DeviceSupport.GuestGpuBackend` now reports one of:
+
+- `ADRENO_KGSL`: upstream Qualcomm path. The KGSL compatibility render node is created only here.
+- `MALI_DRM`: a real `/dev/dri/renderD*` exists and can actually be opened by the app. This is the
+  path on which a glibc PanVK/Panfrost ICD is meaningful.
+- `MALI_PROPRIETARY`: stock Mali exposes `/dev/mali0` but no accessible DRM render node. This path
+  is reserved for the DroidDeck Mali bridge and never fabricates a KGSL-style DRM node.
+- `NONE`: no guest GPU interface available to the app.
+
+The DRM probe opens candidates with `O_RDWR`; merely seeing a node through Android's `/dev` bind is
+not considered sufficient, because SELinux frequently allows stat/list while denying actual use.
+
+### ICD selection and compatibility
+
+- PanVK/Panfrost runtime ICDs are selected automatically only for `MALI_DRM`.
+- Stock `MALI_PROPRIETARY` only auto-selects manifests explicitly named as a DroidDeck Mali bridge.
+- Freedreno/Turnip remains tied to `ADRENO_KGSL`.
+- Imported driver metadata can declare `guestBackend` as `adreno-kgsl`, `mali-drm`, or
+  `mali-proprietary`/`mali-bridge`.
+- Known PanVK/Panfrost imports are refused on `/dev/mali0` phones, and known Turnip/Freedreno imports
+  are refused on Mali. This turns a likely black screen into an explicit compatibility decision.
+
+### Session and diagnostics
+
+Sessions now receive `BL_GUEST_GPU` and, when available, `BL_DRM_RENDER_NODE`. The session log states
+whether the missing component is a PanVK ICD or the proprietary Mali bridge. Device reports include
+the host Vulkan backend, guest GPU backend, and the render node that was actually openable.
+
+Mali telemetry is also best-effort mapped into the existing performance-overlay paths without
+making startup depend on OEM-specific sysfs files.
+
+### Next implementation target
+
+For ordinary unrooted Mali phones the remaining target is `MALI_PROPRIETARY`: implement a guest
+Vulkan ICD whose transport reaches a host-side Android Vulkan service, rather than trying to load a
+bionic vendor HAL into glibc or pretending `/dev/mali0` is DRM. The existing AHardwareBuffer /
+SurfaceControl path should remain the presentation endpoint so the bridge can avoid a CPU readback.
